# .gitignore for a Home Assistant config directory (/homeassistant = HA Core's /config).
# Shipped by the Claude Code add-on: /usr/share/claudecode/git/gitignore — see README.md
# next to it. Copy it to /homeassistant/.gitignore and adapt it; the add-on never edits
# your copy.
#
# The rule: anything that can hold a credential is ignored, and the two directories full
# of them (.storage/ and .claudecode/) are WHITELISTS. A blacklist ("ignore the token
# files") goes wrong silently: every new integration drops its OAuth token into .storage/
# under a name nobody listed. A whitelist goes wrong loudly: a new file is untracked until
# someone adds it (the pre-commit hook, see README.md, catches the one case where that
# hurts: storage dashboards).
#
# ORDER MATTERS. git applies the LAST matching pattern, so the backup-file patterns at the
# bottom must stay below the whitelists, or ".storage/lovelace.<id>.bak" is re-included
# by "!.storage/lovelace.*".

# --- Credentials: never commit -------------------------------------------------------
secrets.yaml
.cloud/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.ssh/
# Add here every file that holds a credential inline instead of through !secret — e.g. the
# YAML config some add-ons keep in the config directory.

# The Claude Code add-on's generated jobs package carries the endpoint bearer token. The
# add-on also puts it in .git/info/exclude on every start; this line covers clones.
/claudecode_jobs.yaml

# --- Claude Code add-on (~/.claude = .claudecode/) ----------------------------------
# OAuth credentials, session transcripts, memory, gh login, job state and logs (job
# notify maps can hold webhook headers). Whitelist only what you write by hand.
/.claudecode/*
!/.claudecode/CLAUDE.user.md
!/.claudecode/jobs/
/.claudecode/jobs/*
!/.claudecode/jobs/*.md
!/.claudecode/skills/
# Claude Code's per-project directory: keep shared settings and skills, not the rest
# (settings.local.json, worktrees, checkpoints, scheduled-task state).
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/skills/
!/.claude/agents/
!/.claude/commands/

# --- .storage: whitelist only safe, valuable files ------------------------------------
# Everything else in .storage holds secrets or churn: auth / auth_provider.* (users,
# password hashes, refresh tokens), core.config_entries + application_credentials (every
# integration's tokens and API keys), cloud, mobile_app (webhook secrets), onboarding,
# the token stores many integrations keep under their own name, hacs.*, traces,
# restore_state. To track something new, add a "!" line — never `git add -f`.
/.storage/*
# Dashboards. The wildcard covers every storage dashboard, so a new one is tracked the day
# it is created (an explicit list silently missed new dashboards). Dashboard configs can
# carry URLs with tokens (iframe / webpage cards) — keep those in a private repo.
!/.storage/lovelace
!/.storage/lovelace.*
!/.storage/lovelace_dashboards
!/.storage/lovelace_resources
# Registries: entity ids, names, areas. device_registry/entity_registry churn on every
# start (modified_at, supported_features) — expected noise in the diffs.
!/.storage/core.area_registry
!/.storage/core.floor_registry
!/.storage/core.label_registry
!/.storage/core.category_registry
!/.storage/core.device_registry
!/.storage/core.entity_registry
# core.config = home location, units, time zone; zone = your saved zones.
!/.storage/core.config
!/.storage/zone
!/.storage/person
!/.storage/homeassistant.exposed_entities
!/.storage/energy
# UI-created helpers
!/.storage/counter
!/.storage/input_boolean
!/.storage/input_button
!/.storage/input_datetime
!/.storage/input_number
!/.storage/input_select
!/.storage/input_text
!/.storage/schedule
!/.storage/timer
!/.storage/tag

# --- Databases, logs, caches, runtime state ------------------------------------------
# *.db* also covers zigbee.db (ZHA: holds the Zigbee network key).
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite*
*.log
*.log.*
home-assistant.log.fault
.ha_run.lock
.cache/
deps/
tts/
backups/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
# ESPHome build cache (configs and esphome/secrets.yaml are handled above)
.esphome/

# --- Backup copies of files (git history replaces them) ------------------------------
# Keep this block LAST: it must win over the .storage whitelist above.
*.bak
*.bak?
*.bak-*
*.session-bak
*.old
*.orig
*~
